          "code": "FORMAT_EXPLORE_CONTENT",
          "id": "1770291602682",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770291602684_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input Data:\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_EXPLORE_MODEL_CONTENT.$output}} \n\n--------------------------------\nDisplay Instructions\n--------------------------------\n- Do NOT Show form, only show paragraph, no widget needs to be added\n- Present the content as readable sections, not as a table.\n- Use clear section headers in CamelCase.\n- Do NOT summarize or invent information.\n- Preserve the content meaning while organizing it into sections.\n- Do NOT output field/value rows.\n- Do NOT output raw JSON or XML.\n- Show Purpose, Required Inputs, and Supported Use Case as pair of Header and Description for it's header\nSomething like, \nPurpose\n<paragraph on purpose>\nRequired Inputs\n<paragraph on required inputs>\nUse Case\n<paragraph on Use case>\n--------------------------------\nActions\n--------------------------------\nAlways include the following two actions at the bottom of the response.\nActions must follow the same structure used for ExploreModel actions.\n\nAction 1:\nora.Invoke(\"CreateModel\", {\n  \"action\": \"CreateModel\",\n  \"model\": \"<modelName>\",\n  \"label\": \"Create <modelName>\"\n})\n\nAction 2:\nora.Invoke(\"ReviewModel\", {\n  \"action\": \"ReviewModel\",\n  \"model\": \"<modelName>\",\n  \"label\": \"Review <modelName>\"\n})\n\n--------------------------------\nRules\n--------------------------------\n- <modelName> must be extracted from the displayed content.\n- Actions must appear only at the bottom.\n- Do NOT mark any action as priority.\n- Do NOT change action names or labels."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
